\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a complete Riemannian manifold satisfying the Ma--Trudinger--Wang curvature condition for squared distance, must every tangent injectivity locus be convex? At $x$, this locus consists of tangent vectors for which the radial geodesic remains minimizing up to its endpoint before the cut locus; convexity is in the vector space $T_xM$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2008/31}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
